1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:08,720
If you've started a GLP-1 weight loss shot like Ozempic or Wegovy, and one eye suddenly gets blurry or part of your vision goes dark, don't brush it off.

2
00:00:09,040 --> 00:00:14,080
That combination can point to NAION, a condition where blood flow to the optic nerve gets cut off.

3
00:00:14,400 --> 00:00:16,880
Doctors sometimes call it a "stroke of the eye."

4
00:00:17,200 --> 00:00:22,000
A 2024 Harvard Medical School study found the risk climbs for a few reasons.

5
00:00:22,320 --> 00:00:30,640
First, patients with diabetes on semaglutide were over four times more likely to be diagnosed with NAION than diabetics who weren't on the drug.

6
00:00:30,960 --> 00:00:38,560
Second, people using it purely for weight loss, without diabetes, showed an even steeper jump - more than seven times the risk.

7
00:00:38,880 --> 00:00:45,600
Researchers haven't proven the drug directly causes this - the study was small, and other health conditions can play a role too.

8
00:00:45,920 --> 00:00:53,920
Still, eye specialists recommend a baseline eye exam before starting, especially if you're over 55 or already have vascular risk factors.

9
00:00:54,240 --> 00:01:00,000
If vision changes hit while you're on the medication, treat it as urgent and get to an eye doctor the same day.

10
00:01:00,320 --> 00:01:04,960
Vision loss from NAION can become permanent, so acting early matters most.
